{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>He who winks</b> — to do evil." "<b>Causes grief</b> — sorrow to his soul. And he said: 'he who winks,' that he fears to do openly, and it is the notion of hinting." "Another interpretation: <b>he who winks</b> — a scoffer." "<b>Causes grief</b> — to his fellow it will burn him if he sees that he mocks him. And one may wish to say, that he does not mean to mock, and will 'move his lips.' [n: וילבטו שפתיו reads literally 'and his lips will move/waver'; possibly corrupt. Rendered hyper-literally.]"], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:52.150180915Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}